<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-task-reminder</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 280 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' __APP_DIR__/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/task-reminder</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Weekdays at 6:45am local — the ONE message the platform still sends
    unprompted (Richard, 2026-10-21). Monday names the tasks with a due date
    this week; Tuesday to Friday send nothing unless something is due THAT DAY
    and is still open.

    ⚠ ONE AGENT, NOT TWO. The route picks the message from the weekday, so
    there is a single schedule to keep in step and no way to double-text
    somebody on a Monday. Which message it would send right now:
    /api/cron/task-reminder?dry=1 — and ?kind=week forces Monday's on any day.

    ⚠ NO MODEL CALL, so it costs the crowded hour nothing: two reads and a
    handful of sends, every figure already a fact.

      06:20  curator          (a read, ~3s)
      06:45  THIS             (two reads, no model)
      06:50  Pepper's note    (HELD 2026-10-21 — returns immediately)
      07:00  daily digest     (still generated and stored; the Chat post is HELD)

    ⚠ A QUIET MORNING STILL WRITES A ROW. `status = 'skipped'` with its reason,
    so /settings/health can tell a clear week from a dead agent — a count that
    has stopped growing cannot (§12).

    ⚠ AND THE SWITCH IS NOT THIS FILE. src/lib/notify/policy.ts decides whether
    anything may be sent; this agent only decides when the question gets asked.
    Keeping it to one switch is deliberate: two that must agree is how a channel
    ends up off while every check reports healthy.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-task-reminder.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-task-reminder.log</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
